tablecloth-wearing Asian...


00:13:00.227 --> 00:13:02.457
- Indian.
- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:13:02.629 --> 00:13:04.392
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:13:05.933 --> 00:13:08.128
Katie, napkin me.


00:13:08.302 --> 00:13:10.793
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:11.205 --> 00:13:14.436
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:14.608 --> 00:13:18.374
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:18.545 --> 00:13:22.174
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:23.116 --> 00:13:25.516
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:25.686 --> 00:13:28.280
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:28.455 --> 00:13:31.322
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:31.492 --> 00:13:32.516
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:32.693 --> 00:13:35.253
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:35.429 --> 00:13:37.363
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:37.531 --> 00:13:40.557
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:40.734 --> 00:13:42.759
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:42.936 --> 00:13:44.904
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:45.072 --> 00:13:46.096
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:46.273 --> 00:13:50.141
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:53.711
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:53.881 --> 00:13:56.975
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:59.448
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:01.554
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:14:01.722 --> 00:14:03.952
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:14:04.124 --> 00:14:07.321
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:07.494 --> 00:14:11.760
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:11.932 --> 00:14:13.900
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:14.401 --> 00:14:17.928
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:20.474 --> 00:14:25.912
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:26.079 --> 00:14:28.639
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:28.815 --> 00:14:30.908
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:31.084 --> 00:14:32.813
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:32.986 --> 00:14:35.614
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:35.789 --> 00:14:39.122
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:39.293 --> 00:14:40.920
Again.


00:14:41.094 --> 00:14:42.652
Really? Okay.


00:14:42.829 --> 00:14:48.461
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:48.635 --> 00:14:49.761
Ouch.


00:14:49.937 --> 00:14:52.997
I could belch the song better.


00:14:54.608 --> 00:14:56.769
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:56.944 --> 00:14:58.411
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:58.579 --> 00:15:01.480
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:15:01.648 --> 00:15:05.550
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:15:05.919 --> 00:15:09.582
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:13.794 --> 00:15:16.160
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:18.059
No.


00:15:18.231 --> 00:15:20.529
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:32.713 --> 00:15:36.012
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:36.183 --> 00:15:38.651
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:49.129 --> 00:15:52.223
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:57.104 --> 00:15:58.833
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:59.006 --> 00:16:00.098
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:16:00.273 --> 00:16:04.369
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:16:04.544 --> 00:16:05.875
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:16:06.046 --> 00:16:08.810
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:09.249 --> 00:16:10.546
Victor!


00:16:10.717 --> 00:16:13.948
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:14.121 --> 00:16:16.282
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:19.793 --> 00:16:21.420
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:31.338 --> 00:16:32.498
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:32.673 --> 00:16:34.072
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:34.241 --> 00:16:37.677
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:37.844 --> 00:16:39.505
Crap.


00:16:42.916 --> 00:16:44.611
This is insane.


00:16:44.785 --> 00:16:48.846
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:58.632 --> 00:17:00.725
You gotta be kidding me.


00:17:02.469 --> 00:17:04.096
Crap.


00:17:07.407 --> 00:17:11.002
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:11.178 --> 00:17:14.978
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:15.148 --> 00:17:17.275
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:17.451 --> 00:17:19.146
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:19.319 --> 00:17:21.879
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:22.055 --> 00:17:25.115
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:25.292 --> 00:17:27.522
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:27.694 --> 00:17:29.821
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:32.165 --> 00:17:33.632
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:39.806 --> 00:17:41.671
Victor.


00:17:45.512 --> 00:17:46.945
Katie?


00:17:48.148 --> 00:17:50.378
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:50.584 --> 00:17:53.849
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:56.784
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:57.824 --> 00:17:59.655
The truth. Um...


00:18:00.961 --> 00:18:04.294
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:18:04.464 --> 00:18:05.795
Naked.


00:18:06.833 --> 00:18:09.131
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:09.302 --> 00:18:10.826
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:13.273 --> 00:18:14.365
There.


00:18:14.541 --> 00:18:17.738
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:22.349 --> 00:18:23.976
I'm kidding.


00:18:24.518 --> 00:18:26.349
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:26.686 --> 00:18:27.710
No, no.


00:18:27.888 --> 00:18:31.289
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:31.458 --> 00:18:33.653
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:34.261 --> 00:18:38.925
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:39.432 --> 00:18:43.232
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:43.403 --> 00:18:45.997
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:49.876 --> 00:18:51.537
What is that?


00:18:52.112 --> 00:18:54.376
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:54.548 --> 00:18:56.516
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:57.717 --> 00:18:59.446
Hey. What...?


00:19:12.299 --> 00:19:14.790
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:14.968 --> 00:19:16.595
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:18.897
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:19.072 --> 00:19:21.336
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:21.508 --> 00:19:22.532
Do you hear this?


00:19:22.709 --> 00:19:24.370
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:24.544 --> 00:19:26.239
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:26.413 --> 00:19:28.745
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:28.915 --> 00:19:31.110
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:31.284 --> 00:19:33.149
She gave you a CD?


00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:36.687
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:37.924 --> 00:19:41.792
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:43.029 --> 00:19:47.125
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:49.102 --> 00:19:51.297
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:52.439 --> 00:19:53.997
So...


00:19:54.875 --> 00:19:57.002
...that meeting today...


00:19:57.177 --> 00:19:59.975
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:20:00.313 --> 00:20:02.372
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:20:02.549 --> 00:20:04.983
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:20:05.252 --> 00:20:06.446
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:07.921 --> 00:20:09.821
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:09.990 --> 00:20:13.118
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:13.393 --> 00:20:17.124
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:22.035 --> 00:20:24.833
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:25.005 --> 00:20:28.065
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:28.241 --> 00:20:30.505
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:34.481 --> 00:20:36.142
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:37.817 --> 00:20:39.114
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:39.286 --> 00:20:42.380
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:42.555 --> 00:20:45.023
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:45.191 --> 00:20:47.352
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:47.527 --> 00:20:48.721
That's interesting.


00:20:48.895 --> 00:20:51.659
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:51.831 --> 00:20:53.059
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:53.233 --> 00:20:54.860
I only have cheese.


00:20:58.038 --> 00:21:00.006
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:21:00.173 --> 00:21:02.073
Your phone.


00:21:05.111 --> 00:21:07.978
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:08.148 --> 00:21:09.706
I have underestimated you.


00:21:10.283 --> 00:21:12.114
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:12.285 --> 00:21:15.379
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:15.555 --> 00:21:18.183
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:18.358 --> 00:21:22.556
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:22.729 --> 00:21:25.994
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:26.166 --> 00:21:29.602
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:29.769 --> 00:21:32.897
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:33.073 --> 00:21:38.204
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:39.479 --> 00:21:41.640
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:47.053 --> 00:21:51.683
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:51.858 --> 00:21:55.954
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:56.129 --> 00:21:59.895
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:22:00.367 --> 00:22:02.028
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:22:02.202 --> 00:22:04.363
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:07.607 --> 00:22:10.303
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:10.877 --> 00:22:14.335
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:14.781 --> 00:22:16.749
I like trouble.


00:22:18.284 --> 00:22:19.410
Hey, kids.


00:22:20.720 --> 00:22:24.156
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:24.324 --> 00:22:27.088
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:31.094
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:31.398 --> 00:22:36.631
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:36.836 --> 00:22:39.304
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:39.572 --> 00:22:42.132
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:42.308 --> 00:22:44.276
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:44.444 --> 00:22:47.504
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:47.680 --> 00:22:50.740
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:50.917 --> 00:22:53.613
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:53.787 --> 00:22:57.086
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:57.257 --> 00:22:59.088
What if I don't want to?


00:23:00.193 --> 00:23:03.924
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:23:04.097 --> 00:23:06.156
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:23:06.332 --> 00:23:08.596
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:08.768 --> 00:23:12.329
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:12.505 --> 00:23:13.995
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:14.174 --> 00:23:15.641
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:17.243 --> 00:23:19.370
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:19.546 --> 00:23:22.674
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:23.083 --> 00:23:27.281
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:27.454 --> 00:23:31.288
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:31.458 --> 00:23:34.359
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:34.527 --> 00:23:36.791
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:36.963 --> 00:23:39.090
You are a star.


00:23:39.265 --> 00:23:43.463
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:43.636 --> 00:23:45.194
I'm a star.


00:23:45.371 --> 00:23:49.535
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:49.709 --> 00:23:52.109
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:52.278 --> 00:23:54.246
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:54.414 --> 00:23:55.972
Every part of him.


00:23:56.149 --> 00:23:59.676
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:23:59.853 --> 00:24:02.617
And just leave me out of this.


00:24:03.890 --> 00:24:06.450
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:06.626 --> 00:24:08.526
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:09.129 --> 00:24:11.029
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:11.197 --> 00:24:13.893
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:14.067 --> 00:24:16.126
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:16.302 --> 00:24:17.667
Are we clear?


00:24:18.104 --> 00:24:19.298
Crystal.


00:24:21.241 --> 00:24:24.233
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:24.410 --> 00:24:28.403
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:28.581 --> 00:24:31.049
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:31.217 --> 00:24:32.548
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:32.719 --> 00:24:34.846
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:35.021 --> 00:24:36.545
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:36.723 --> 00:24:40.090
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:40.260 --> 00:24:42.956
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:43.129 --> 00:24:45.393
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:45.565 --> 00:24:47.123
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:47.300 --> 00:24:49.427
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:49.602 --> 00:24:51.069
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:51.237 --> 00:24:54.070
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:54.240 --> 00:24:56.902
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:57.076 --> 00:24:58.839
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:59.012 --> 00:25:00.707
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:25:01.147 --> 00:25:03.843
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:25:04.017 --> 00:25:06.747
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:06.920 --> 00:25:08.114
We're here to impress.


00:25:08.288 --> 00:25:10.552
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:14.394 --> 00:25:16.862
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:17.030 --> 00:25:19.294
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:19.465 --> 00:25:21.660
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:21.834 --> 00:25:25.201
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:25.371 --> 00:25:27.896
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:28.074 --> 00:25:31.339
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:31.511 --> 00:25:36.813
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:36.983 --> 00:25:43.718
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:44.924 --> 00:25:46.414
That's good.


00:25:53.466 --> 00:25:56.765
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:57.604 --> 00:25:59.936
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:26:00.106 --> 00:26:02.006
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:26:03.042 --> 00:26:06.637
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:06.813 --> 00:26:09.008
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:09.182 --> 00:26:11.116
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:11.284 --> 00:26:16.517
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:16.689 --> 00:26:18.884
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:19.425 --> 00:26:21.188
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:21.361 --> 00:26:23.955
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:24.564 --> 00:26:27.863
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:28.034 --> 00:26:29.501
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:29.669 --> 00:26:31.694
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:31.871 --> 00:26:34.863
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:37.043 --> 00:26:39.477
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:43.016 --> 00:26:44.847
Okay.


00:26:45.418 --> 00:26:47.784
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:48.121 --> 00:26:49.884
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:50.056 --> 00:26:52.047
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:52.225 --> 00:26:54.056
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:54.227 --> 00:26:56.525
That I shall not cross.


00:26:56.996 --> 00:26:59.294
So sing something.


00:27:00.967 --> 00:27:02.434
Okay.


00:27:06.572 --> 00:27:09.370
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:09.542 --> 00:27:12.033
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:12.211 --> 00:27:13.610
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:14.080 --> 00:27:16.071
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:17.884 --> 00:27:20.352
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:20.520 --> 00:27:23.045
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:23.222 --> 00:27:24.814
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:25.325 --> 00:27:26.952
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:27.960 --> 00:27:30.895
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:31.064 --> 00:27:33.396
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:33.566 --> 00:27:35.033
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:36.436 --> 00:27:38.097
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:39.038 --> 00:27:41.871
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:42.041 --> 00:27:47.240
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:47.413 --> 00:27:48.971
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:50.083 --> 00:27:52.677
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:52.852 --> 00:27:55.412
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:55.588 --> 00:27:59.957
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:28:01.361 --> 00:28:04.023
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:28:04.197 --> 00:28:06.461
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:06.632 --> 00:28:09.294
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:09.469 --> 00:28:11.960
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:16.442 --> 00:28:18.569
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:18.745 --> 00:28:21.373
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:21.547 --> 00:28:24.880
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:25.151 --> 00:28:27.642
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:27.820 --> 00:28:29.811
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:29.989 --> 00:28:32.287
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:32.458 --> 00:28:34.153
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:34.427 --> 00:28:36.122
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:36.562 --> 00:28:40.396
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:40.867 --> 00:28:44.963
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:45.138 --> 00:28:46.162
...good acoustics.


00:28:46.572 --> 00:28:50.406
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:50.576 --> 00:28:52.168
If you gave them your song.


00:28:53.579 --> 00:28:55.240
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:55.982 --> 00:28:58.678
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:58.851 --> 00:29:00.182
Yeah.


00:29:01.854 --> 00:29:08.384
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:08.694 --> 00:29:09.991
You wrote that song today?


00:29:10.163 --> 00:29:13.621
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:13.900 --> 00:29:15.197
You really like this guy.


00:29:15.368 --> 00:29:17.063
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:17.236 --> 00:29:19.431
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:19.605 --> 00:29:23.097
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:24.911 --> 00:29:27.709
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:31.317 --> 00:29:34.150
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:36.189 --> 00:29:38.657
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:38.991 --> 00:29:42.483
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:42.662 --> 00:29:44.687
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:44.864 --> 00:29:45.888
Am not.


00:29:46.933 --> 00:29:49.925
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:50.102 --> 00:29:52.798
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:52.972 --> 00:29:55.532
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:55.708 --> 00:29:58.404
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:58.578 --> 00:30:00.512
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:30:00.680 --> 00:30:04.707
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:30:05.084 --> 00:30:08.178
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:11.123 --> 00:30:12.647
Okay.


00:30:12.959 --> 00:30:14.551
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:14.727 --> 00:30:16.058
That's my girl.


00:30:16.329 --> 00:30:20.322
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:20.500 --> 00:30:23.799
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:23.970 --> 00:30:25.733
What? Why?


00:30:25.905 --> 00:30:27.270
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:31.177 --> 00:30:32.735
Katie!


00:30:32.912 --> 00:30:36.348
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:36.516 --> 00:30:38.006
Go.


00:30:38.184 --> 00:30:39.913
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:40.086 --> 00:30:41.417
Angie, heads up.


00:30:43.389 --> 00:30:44.686
Katie!


00:30:49.896 --> 00:30:51.625
What's going on?


00:30:51.797 --> 00:30:53.230
Nothing.


00:30:53.399 --> 00:30:56.527
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:56.702 --> 00:30:59.000
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:59.171 --> 00:31:03.232
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:31:06.479 --> 00:31:10.643
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:10.816 --> 00:31:13.046
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:13.219 --> 00:31:14.652
Oh, no, no.


00:31:14.820 --> 00:31:17.311
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:17.490 --> 00:31:19.788
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:19.959 --> 00:31:22.655
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:22.828 --> 00:31:23.852
Fun.


00:31:24.030 --> 00:31:27.158
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:27.333 --> 00:31:30.734
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:31.604 --> 00:31:33.629
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:37.610 --> 00:31:39.976
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:40.313 --> 00:31:42.577
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:42.882 --> 00:31:45.976
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:46.252 --> 00:31:49.415
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:49.755 --> 00:31:52.815
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:52.992 --> 00:31:55.392
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:55.561 --> 00:31:58.496
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:58.664 --> 00:32:02.691
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:32:02.969 --> 00:32:06.268
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:07.473 --> 00:32:08.770
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:18.751 --> 00:32:21.015
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:21.187 --> 00:32:23.382
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:23.990 --> 00:32:27.016
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:28.194 --> 00:32:31.322
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:32.098 --> 00:32:34.362
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:34.533 --> 00:32:36.831
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:37.003 --> 00:32:40.200
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:43.409 --> 00:32:46.037
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:46.212 --> 00:32:49.272
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:49.448 --> 00:32:52.645
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:53.552 --> 00:32:56.419
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:56.589 --> 00:32:58.648
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:58.824 --> 00:32:59.916
I'm talking to Luke.


00:33:00.526 --> 00:33:03.017
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:33:03.195 --> 00:33:04.662
...before Gail gets here.


00:33:05.398 --> 00:33:06.729
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:06.899 --> 00:33:07.923
Mm-hm.


00:33:08.100 --> 00:33:09.499
Right.


00:33:10.503 --> 00:33:11.902
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:14.974 --> 00:33:16.236
Hmm.


00:33:21.047 --> 00:33:23.038
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:23.716 --> 00:33:24.740
Ravi?


00:33:26.419 --> 00:33:28.944
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:29.121 --> 00:33:31.555
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:33.693 --> 00:33:36.253
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:36.429 --> 00:33:37.623
Obviously.


00:33:38.164 --> 00:33:40.655
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:40.833 --> 00:33:42.391
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:42.568 --> 00:33:45.935
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:46.472 --> 00:33:49.600
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:49.775 --> 00:33:52.437
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:52.812 --> 00:33:56.213
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:56.382 --> 00:33:58.247
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:58.617 --> 00:34:00.141
But I never got my shot.


00:34:00.319 --> 00:34:02.549
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:34:02.722 --> 00:34:05.122
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:34:05.291 --> 00:34:07.486
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:07.660 --> 00:34:09.150
"Who is asking?"


00:34:09.428 --> 00:34:12.795
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:12.965 --> 00:34:15.559
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:15.735 --> 00:34:20.104
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:20.406 --> 00:34:22.670
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:22.842 --> 00:34:25.242
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:25.578 --> 00:34:28.206
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:28.380 --> 00:34:29.574
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:30.783 --> 00:34:33.479
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:36.288 --> 00:34:39.951
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:40.626 --> 00:34:42.685
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:42.862 --> 00:34:45.330
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:45.498 --> 00:34:46.556
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:48.134 --> 00:34:49.465
Blow it up.


00:34:51.403 --> 00:34:52.961
Thank you.


00:35:02.782 --> 00:35:04.181
Whoa.


00:35:04.350 --> 00:35:06.978
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:07.153 --> 00:35:10.213
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:11.590 --> 00:35:13.922
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:14.093 --> 00:35:17.324
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:20.032 --> 00:35:23.001
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:23.169 --> 00:35:26.798
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:27.506 --> 00:35:29.838
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:35.214 --> 00:35:36.647
Where is he?


00:35:37.483 --> 00:35:40.281
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:40.452 --> 00:35:42.113
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:42.288 --> 00:35:44.722
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:48.227 --> 00:35:51.788
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:51.964 --> 00:35:55.297
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:55.467 --> 00:35:57.662
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:57.870 --> 00:36:00.600
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:36:00.773 --> 00:36:03.207
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:10.015 --> 00:36:11.073
I think I found him.


00:36:11.250 --> 00:36:13.514
Well, he is blond.


00:36:16.622 --> 00:36:18.920
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:20.826 --> 00:36:23.124
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:23.295 --> 00:36:24.694
What are you doing here?


00:36:24.864 --> 00:36:27.697
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:27.867 --> 00:36:29.892
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:30.069 --> 00:36:33.004
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:33.172 --> 00:36:35.003
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:35.174 --> 00:36:37.642
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:40.079 --> 00:36:42.206
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:43.749 --> 00:36:47.185
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:47.353 --> 00:36:49.548
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:49.722 --> 00:36:52.589
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:52.758 --> 00:36:54.692
...and you're fired.


00:36:57.730 --> 00:37:01.257
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:37:03.869 --> 00:37:05.359
I heard you sing at school.


00:37:05.604 --> 00:37:06.730
You were amazing.


00:37:06.906 --> 00:37:07.964
Do I know you?


00:37:12.311 --> 00:37:14.905
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:17.249 --> 00:37:19.308
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:19.952 --> 00:37:22.443
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:26.959 --> 00:37:29.792
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:29.962 --> 00:37:31.327
Miss Van R.


00:37:31.964 --> 00:37:34.364
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:34.533 --> 00:37:35.727
...but were never good enough?


00:37:37.102 --> 00:37:38.763
Who told you that?


00:37:56.488 --> 00:37:57.921
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:58.090 --> 00:38:01.287
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:38:01.460 --> 00:38:02.586
Oh!


00:38:02.761 --> 00:38:06.993
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:11.337 --> 00:38:14.431
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:14.606 --> 00:38:17.507
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:22.281 --> 00:38:25.011
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:25.351 --> 00:38:28.047
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:28.220 --> 00:38:29.482
Follow me.


00:38:34.526 --> 00:38:36.357
Oh, wow.


00:38:38.831 --> 00:38:44.394
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:45.270 --> 00:38:47.170
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:47.339 --> 00:38:51.036
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:52.544 --> 00:38:53.738
Or not.


00:38:56.015 --> 00:38:59.041
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:39:05.257 --> 00:39:08.818
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:10.129 --> 00:39:14.361
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:14.533 --> 00:39:18.060
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:18.237 --> 00:39:22.230
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:24.209 --> 00:39:27.542
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:29.314 --> 00:39:33.011
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:33.685 --> 00:39:37.382
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:37.856 --> 00:39:40.689
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:41.160 --> 00:39:42.252
Uh-uh.


00:42:21.186 --> 00:42:23.780
I think I've blown something.


00:42:23.956 --> 00:42:27.016
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:29.628 --> 00:42:31.186
Move it, fatso.


00:42:32.931 --> 00:42:39.530
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:40.272 --> 00:42:43.901
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:56.455 --> 00:42:57.888
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:58.056 --> 00:43:00.081
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:43:00.259 --> 00:43:02.819
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:43:02.995 --> 00:43:04.963
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:07.432 --> 00:43:08.797
I'm so sorry.


00:43:09.501 --> 00:43:10.729
What...? You...?


00:43:11.436 --> 00:43:13.097
Hey. Wait.


00:43:13.272 --> 00:43:14.500
But who are you?


00:43:14.673 --> 00:43:17.267
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:25.417 --> 00:43:28.443
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:46.905 --> 00:43:48.930
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:49.708 --> 00:43:52.643
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:53.078 --> 00:43:56.013
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:56.348 --> 00:43:58.543
Don't talk about her like that.


00:44:00.552 --> 00:44:03.715
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:44:03.889 --> 00:44:07.450
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:07.626 --> 00:44:09.890
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:10.062 --> 00:44:13.122
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:13.432 --> 00:44:16.560
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:17.469 --> 00:44:20.597
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:27.112 --> 00:44:30.343
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:30.515 --> 00:44:32.574
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:32.751 --> 00:44:34.685
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:34.853 --> 00:44:36.548
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:36.722 --> 00:44:39.020
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:40.392 --> 00:44:44.522
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:45.497 --> 00:44:49.092
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:50.168 --> 00:44:51.795
We're recording.


00:44:52.104 --> 00:44:53.935
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:54.106 --> 00:44:55.334
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:55.941 --> 00:44:57.875
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:58.043 --> 00:44:59.772
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:44:59.945 --> 00:45:02.277
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:45:02.447 --> 00:45:03.675
Check this out, all right?


00:45:03.849 --> 00:45:07.444
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:07.619 --> 00:45:09.450
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:09.621 --> 00:45:11.452
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:11.656 --> 00:45:13.681
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:13.859 --> 00:45:15.019
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:15.193 --> 00:45:17.161
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:17.329 --> 00:45:19.194
That was subpar at best.


00:45:19.364 --> 00:45:21.889
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:22.634 --> 00:45:25.933
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:26.104 --> 00:45:27.662
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:27.839 --> 00:45:30.205
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:30.375 --> 00:45:33.401
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:33.578 --> 00:45:36.672
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:36.848 --> 00:45:38.406
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:38.850 --> 00:45:41.717
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:42.254 --> 00:45:45.815
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:46.091 --> 00:45:49.424
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:49.594 --> 00:45:52.188
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:52.364 --> 00:45:54.832
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:55.000 --> 00:45:58.094
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:58.270 --> 00:46:00.795
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:46:02.541 --> 00:46:07.137
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:07.312 --> 00:46:10.281
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:10.449 --> 00:46:13.282
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:19.324 --> 00:46:22.521
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:41.646 --> 00:46:43.944
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:44.115 --> 00:46:45.309
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:45.484 --> 00:46:47.782
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:47.953 --> 00:46:49.318
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:50.155 --> 00:46:52.282
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:52.457 --> 00:46:53.583
This is not good.


00:46:55.160 --> 00:46:56.957
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:57.128 --> 00:46:58.959
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:59.130 --> 00:47:01.530
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:47:01.700 --> 00:47:05.136
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:47:05.303 --> 00:47:06.327
Listen...


00:47:06.505 --> 00:47:09.941
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:10.108 --> 00:47:11.769
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:23.622 --> 00:47:27.615
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:27.792 --> 00:47:30.784
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:30.962 --> 00:47:34.591
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:34.766 --> 00:47:38.702
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:38.870 --> 00:47:42.670
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:43.208 --> 00:47:46.109
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:46.278 --> 00:47:49.338
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:51.149 --> 00:47:53.083
It was you?


00:47:53.752 --> 00:47:56.846
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:57.789 --> 00:48:01.623
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:48:03.261 --> 00:48:06.287
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:48:06.464 --> 00:48:09.228
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:09.401 --> 00:48:11.528
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:12.170 --> 00:48:14.900
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:15.173 --> 00:48:16.936
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:17.108 --> 00:48:20.475
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:20.645 --> 00:48:22.909
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:24.416 --> 00:48:26.213
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:26.384 --> 00:48:27.476
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:28.420 --> 00:48:29.887
You have a date with detention.


00:48:30.055 --> 00:48:31.522
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:31.690 --> 00:48:33.419
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:33.592 --> 00:48:36.288
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:36.461 --> 00:48:39.589
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:39.764 --> 00:48:41.254
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:41.433 --> 00:48:43.333
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:43.501 --> 00:48:46.299
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:46.471 --> 00:48:48.837
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:49.007 --> 00:48:50.474
Fine.


00:48:51.276 --> 00:48:52.800
I hate you.


00:48:56.448 --> 00:49:00.578
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:49:00.852 --> 00:49:02.786
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:09.361 --> 00:49:10.988
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:11.162 --> 00:49:14.359
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:14.532 --> 00:49:15.999
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:16.167 --> 00:49:18.965
Chores. Bores. Sores.


00:49:19.137 --> 00:49:21.332
Katie, I've got a new task for you.


